---
// InfoSection.astro
---

<section id="features" class="border-t border-slate-200/80 bg-white py-16 transition-colors dark:border-slate-800/80 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Powerful, Private, and 100% Free QR Code Generator
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Generate professional QR codes for marketing campaigns, store menus, business cards, Wi-Fi sharing, and navigation with zero watermarks or expiry dates.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <!-- Feature 1 -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-6 transition-all hover:shadow-md dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
        <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-100 text-blue-600 dark:bg-blue-900/40 dark:text-blue-400">
          <svg class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="3" rx="2"></rect>
            <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="2"></circle>
            <path d="m21 15-3.086-3.086a2 2 0 0 0-2.828 0L6 21"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Custom Logo Overlay</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Embed your brand or social icon in the center of the QR code. Automatic error correction boost (Level H) ensures reliable scannability.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 2 -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-6 transition-all hover:shadow-md dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
        <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-600 dark:bg-indigo-900/40 dark:text-indigo-400">
          <svg class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"></polyline>
            <polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"></polyline>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">High-Resolution Vector SVG & PNG</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Download print-ready raster PNG (1200×1200px) or infinite-resolution SVG vectors ready for billboards, merchandise, and print media.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 3 -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-6 transition-all hover:shadow-md dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
        <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-600 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 dark:text-emerald-400">
          <svg class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">100% Private & Browser-Based</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          No data is stored or transmitted. The QR code generation runs entirely within your web browser using open-source algorithms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 4 -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-6 transition-all hover:shadow-md dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
        <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-100 text-amber-600 dark:bg-amber-900/40 dark:text-amber-400">
          <svg class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M20 10c0 6-8 12-8 12s-8-6-8-12a8 8 0 0 1 16 0Z"></path>
            <circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"></circle>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">GPS Location (geo: URI)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Encode exact latitude and longitude coordinates. When scanned, smartphones open Apple Maps, Google Maps, or native navigation apps.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 5 -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-6 transition-all hover:shadow-md dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
        <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-600 dark:bg-cyan-900/40 dark:text-cyan-400">
          <svg class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M5 12.55a11 11 0 0 1 14.08 0"></path>
            <path d="M1.42 9a16 16 0 0 1 21.16 0"></path>
            <path d="M8.53 16.11a6 6 0 0 1 6.95 0"></path>
            <line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12.01" y2="20"></line>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">One-Tap Wi-Fi Join</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Generate Wi-Fi codes for guests, customers, and offices. Guests can scan with their phone camera to connect without typing complex passwords.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 6 -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-6 transition-all hover:shadow-md dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
        <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-rose-100 text-rose-600 dark:bg-rose-900/40 dark:text-rose-400">
          <svg class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="13.5" cy="6.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle>
            <circle cx="17.5" cy="10.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle>
            <circle cx="8.5" cy="7.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle>
            <circle cx="6.5" cy="12.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle>
            <path d="M12 2C6.5 2 2 6.5 2 12s4.5 10 10 10c.926 0 1.648-.746 1.648-1.688 0-.437-.18-.835-.437-1.125-.29-.289-.438-.652-.438-1.125a1.64 1.64 0 0 1 1.668-1.668h1.996c3.051 0 5.563-2.512 5.563-5.563C22 6.5 17.5 2 12 2Z"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Custom Brand Colors</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Tailor foreground and background colors to match your brand guide or packaging. Built-in contrast helper keeps the code easy to scan.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    <div id="faq" class="mt-20 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-center">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Do these QR codes ever expire?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            No! All QR codes generated here are static QR codes. The destination URL or information is encoded directly into the pixel pattern, meaning they will work permanently and never stop working.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Which error correction level should I choose?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            <strong>Level L (7%)</strong> creates the simplest, lowest density QR code (best for long URLs on small screens). <strong>Level M (15%)</strong> is the standard default for most uses. <strong>Level Q (25%)</strong> and <strong>Level H (30%)</strong> are recommended if you are embedding a logo or printing in outdoor environments where the code might get slightly scuffed or obstructed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How does the Location QR code work?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            It produces a standard <code>geo:latitude,longitude</code> URI (RFC 5870). When scanned by modern smartphones (iOS Camera or Android Google Lens), it immediately prompts to open the location in Google Maps, Apple Maps, or Waze.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/50 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Can I use these QR codes for commercial projects?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Yes, 100%. You can use the generated PNG and SVG QR codes for retail products, restaurant menus, flyers, business cards, books, packaging, and commercial advertisements free of charge.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
